# [Perf] [AMD] hyperconnection: Add a Triton prefill path for gated HC sites
# https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/50863  (PR head 11f2ab45fc)
# Generated against the 20261117 image's SGLang checkout (c67db7c762) with patches 01-07, 09, 11, 13-16, 21, 24 and 23
# applied; source files only (tests, docs and the benchmark dropped).
# Replaces patch 15 (an earlier revision of this PR, opt-in SGLANG_AMD_HC_PREFILL) by the PR head: this patch turns
# patch 15's two files into the head's and adds the head's other source changes. Opt-in
# SGLANG_USE_HIP_HC_PREFILL_TRITON=1 (gfx950): gated HC sites with a per-branch norm of more than 48 rows run on the raw
# residual as Triton kernels, the down projection a split-K kernel up to 512 rows and a batched GEMM above. Patch 15's
# variables (SGLANG_AMD_HC_PREFILL, SGLANG_AMD_HC_FUSED_MAX_M, SGLANG_AMD_HC_PREFILL_MAX_M) are no longer read.
# Port: the PR targets main, which lacks sglang#48648 (patch 01). Here the Triton path is tried before 01's fused
# decode-sized mix, and the fused mix leaves the Triton path's rows alone, so with the variable set the fused path
# serves 1-48 rows and the Triton path the rest; a combine tells the two paths' residuals (neither has a normed
# residual) apart by the row count. Unset, 01's fused path serves 1-128 rows as before.
# Apply in /sgl-workspace/sglang with git apply.

